From: Li Guan <guanli.oerv@isrc.iscas.ac.cn>
Subject: [PATCH] Preserve Ant arguments with a Java launcher argument file

TestNG's default test name contains a space. JCommander's argument-file
reader splits each line at whitespace, causing the second word to be
treated as an XML suite filename. Pass a quoted argument file to the Java
launcher, including the main class, so names and paths retain their
boundaries while keeping support for long command lines.

Signed-off-by: Li Guan <guanli.oerv@isrc.iscas.ac.cn>
---
--- a/src/main/java/org/testng/TestNGAntTask.java
+++ b/src/main/java/org/testng/TestNGAntTask.java
@@ -513,8 +513,13 @@
       }
       fw = new FileWriter(f);
       bw = new BufferedWriter(fw);
+      bw.write(m_mainClass);
+      bw.newLine();
       for (String arg : argv) {
-        bw.write(arg);
+        bw.write("\"");
+        bw.write(arg.replace("\\", "\\\\").replace("\"", "\\\"")
+            .replace("\n", "\\n").replace("\r", "\\r").replace("\t", "\\t"));
+        bw.write("\"");
         bw.newLine();
       }
       bw.flush();
@@ -537,7 +542,7 @@
 
     createClasspath().setLocation(findJar());
 
-    cmd.createArgument().setValue("@" + fileName);
+    cmd.setClassname("@" + fileName);
 
     ExecuteWatchdog watchdog = createWatchdog();
     boolean wasKilled = false;
